{"kind":"event","event_id":7159,"event_uid":"01M2NQQN3S7JF1Q317VAGQ3ZRH","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":306,"issue_uid":"01M2NQMSQGBGHESXHBPV7S57B5","issue_short_id":"57b5","actor":"impl:2@run-166","hlc_physical_ms":1789583414393,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"ae8535eb244be3b10df0bb27841ecbd53abc457b72987d2210bf0b1fffcff4a9","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2NQQN3RDPNBKGCK3XBYB7GT","author":"impl:2@run-166","body":"Approach for Task 2 (fold census): a single python3-stdlib script at skills/ultrapowers/scripts/fold_census.py, house style off fleet_events.py (module docstring, _outcome.swallow for deliberate skips, 'fold_census: ' stderr prefix, argparse under __main__). Wave discovery: run/frontier/wave-<n> named '<n>' then run/publish-fold/frontier/wave-<a> named 'publish-<a>', each group numerically sorted, frontier group first. shape_of(kind, narration) is the whole of M2 for one entry and is pure-string so the exam can call it directly. census_run(run_dir) returns the --json object ({run, waves, totals}); both the table and the --json stream render off it, so M1 and M4 cannot drift. Every read is wrapped: an unreadable conflicts.json / fold_log.jsonl is one stderr line and a count of zero.","created_at":"2026-09-16T18:30:14.392283011Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T18:30:14.393Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":7160,"event_uid":"01M2NQR5BW96X0BFEWMY9RC13S","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":306,"issue_uid":"01M2NQMSQGBGHESXHBPV7S57B5","issue_short_id":"57b5","actor":"exam:2@run-166","hlc_physical_ms":1789583431036,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"850cbd10a4636431c37640cd68375441bd8a0a83430ef366403f20e063541483","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2NQR5BTGH7CRF19K1J2ER99","author":"exam:2@run-166","body":"examiner (task 2, exam round 1): approach for tests/test_fold_census.py.\n\nOne fixture builder for the five-entry run-7 wave the Proof's (b)/(c) pin (i=1 insert-only epoch 3, i=2 overlapping epoch 5, i=3 binary, i=4 delete/modify, i=5 parked-with-reason-line-only), hand-written per the Context's narration rules rather than produced by the kernel. The script is driven with subprocess.run([sys.executable, SCRIPT, ...]) in the style of tests/test_authoring_census.py; the two Produces symbols (census_run, shape_of) are imported once through importlib.util.spec_from_file_location for leg (g).\n\nLeg by leg: (a) header's eleven fields and argv order; (b) the five shapes through --json plus a sixth run dir for the deleted-only 'lines' entry; (c) dispatches 3 / retries 1 / resolved 1 / parked 3 with the per-conflict 2/1/true, 1/0/false, 0/0/false; (d) publish-fold wave named publish-1 and the both-records run summing to waves 2; (e) empty dir zeros, a '{' conflicts.json as one stderr line still counted in waves at exit 0, a non-directory at exit 2; (f) exact key sets; (g) shape_of/census_run; (i) --help names --json.\n\nReadings I am pinning, from the task's own words: the table is split on whitespace (Context), so the exam never asserts the two-space join as bytes; 'unclassified' is in 'conflicts' and in none of the four shape columns (M2), so run-7's conflicts is 5 while the four columns sum to 4; parked is dispatchable-false and is independent of shape (M3), so the binary and delete/modify entries count parked too.","created_at":"2026-09-16T18:30:31.034933168Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T18:30:31.036Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":7161,"event_uid":"01M2NQRW5K0JCY43RJSMN2A6V9","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":305,"issue_uid":"01M2NQMNMQTF23T4BBJXT37RY3","issue_short_id":"7ry3","actor":"impl:1@run-166","hlc_physical_ms":1789583454387,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"d857024f7ca50143516f74d294b39270cd31a6a85a462763ee73fc5741bab85c","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2NQRW5HS2ZY0P5VZ90AD799","author":"impl:1@run-166","body":"Approach: add EVIDENCE_FILE_MAX=\"${FLEET_EVIDENCE_FILE_MAX:-1048576}\" beside COMMIT_EVENTS (fleet/sandbox-boot.sh ~line 162), and a frontier/ walk in collect_evidence modelled on the state-exams walk: find \"$run_dir/frontier\" -type f -not -path '*/frontier/weave/blobs/*', rel-rebuild under $dest/frontier, tolerant cp, size measured with wc -c <\"$f\" (no stat).\n\nOne wrinkle the task text forces: collect_evidence runs at EVERY write_status transition and once more at fail, so a naive skip log would emit the over-cap line once per transition, while M3/leg (d) demand EXACTLY ONE line. Deduping against the boot log itself (grep -qF \"evidence: frontier/$rel is \" \"$BOOT_LOG\") keeps the once-ever property with no new state file and nothing extra on the record.","created_at":"2026-09-16T18:30:54.385887160Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T18:30:54.387Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":7162,"event_uid":"01M2NQV8K1T08K19SZJ2N9MW8J","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":305,"issue_uid":"01M2NQMNMQTF23T4BBJXT37RY3","issue_short_id":"7ry3","actor":"exam:1@run-166","hlc_physical_ms":1789583532641,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"73dc2d61c3fbfb091ba0170bf33d51fc4e639fdd442ce02e472a6c1a153b24fb","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2NQV8K0FD384W1GGVFQC12Z","author":"exam:1@run-166","body":"examiner (task 1), approach for `fleet/tests/test_sandbox_boot_fold_record.mjs`:\n\nTwo boots of the `_sandbox_boot_helpers.mjs` rig, each started once with `bootAsync` and shared by every leg that reads it (a boot is ~40 forks of stub shell):\n\n- KEPT (default cap) — seeds, under `runDir(ctx)` before the boot, the nine files M1 names plus `frontier/weave/blobs/<64 hex>` and a 1048577-byte `frontier/wave-1/conflict-2.txt`. Legs (a) (b) (c) (d) read it.\n- CAP64 — `FLEET_EVIDENCE_FILE_MAX=64`, seeds `frontier/wave-1/reply-1-1/h1.txt` at exactly 64 bytes and `notes.txt` at 65. Leg (e) reads it.\n\nReadings a later session would otherwise have to reconstruct:\n\n1. Leg (d) says `stream(ctx)` carries EXACTLY ONE line matching the skip, and M3 says the boot log carries ONE line naming the file. `collect_evidence` runs at every `write_status` transition and once more at `fail`, so a walk that logs unconditionally emits that line once per transition. I am encoding the leg as written — `assert.deepEqual(skips, [<the one line>])` — because `one line` is what both M3 and the leg say. It is satisfiable: the boot is one bash process, so the copy can remember what it has already named (a file of reported paths under `$FLEET_HOME`, or a shell variable) and log each skipped path once per run. Same for leg (e)'s `one skip line`.\n2. Leg (a) additionally asserts the evidence `frontier/` tree is EXACTLY the nine relative paths. That is M1 + M2 + M3 over this seeding and nothing more: the walk copies only what is under `$run_dir/frontier`, blobs are excluded by M2 and the oversize file by M3, so nine is the whole set. It also carries the `no frontier/frontier entry` clause, which is asserted separately by name as well.\n3. Legs (g) and (h) are the Proof's second and third `Run:` lines, run verbatim inside the sim with `spawnSync('bash', ['-c', …], { cwd: ROOT, env: ENV })`, the way `test_sandbox_boot_disclosures.mjs` runs its readers. Leg (h)'s path is interpolated from `import.meta.url` rather than spelled as a literal, so the hermetic probe's `sibling` rule (`test_[a-z0-9_]+\\.mjs` in a spawn's call text) does not read the sim naming itself as a sibling run. The command bash sees is character-identical to the Proof's.\n4. Leg (f) — `the sim prints the sentinel` — is the aggregate of (a)–(e); its own assertion pins that the runner this sim hands its cases to prints the exact sentinel the first `Run:` greps for.\n\nExpected red at BASE: no `frontier` directory reaches the evidence worktree at all, and the CONTRACT range carries neither `weave/blobs` nor `FLEET_EVIDENCE_FILE_MAX`.","created_at":"2026-09-16T18:32:12.640086036Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T18:32:12.641Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":7163,"event_uid":"01M2NQXPZG9EKWA906D1KTD899","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":306,"issue_uid":"01M2NQMSQGBGHESXHBPV7S57B5","issue_short_id":"57b5","actor":"impl:2@run-166","hlc_physical_ms":1789583612912,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"e743385ce62507f8a686057118dd9592d16670a6b0640d9e6f3cd29db05ee66c","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2NQXPZE2CQ2QXV8GATSQYY8","author":"impl:2@run-166","body":"Done. skills/ultrapowers/scripts/fold_census.py + tests/test_fold_census.py, all four PROOFS green (16 tests pass; --help names --json; the kernel/engine diff is empty; the sims-are-hermetic suite passes). Readings a later session would otherwise re-derive: (1) wave order is the copied frontier's waves numerically, then the publish fold's, so a run with both reads ['1','publish-1']; (2) M3's wave-level 'dispatches' counts every reply-<i>-<attempt>/ directory in the wave (the per-conflict field counts only those whose <i> matches), which agrees with the per-conflict sums on leg (c)'s fixture and is the literal reading; (3) shape_of returns 'unclassified' for a marker set that is neither all-added, all-deleted, nor both — a kind outside hunks.py's {added,deleted} vocabulary buckets nowhere, same as a narration with no markers; (4) M5's 'one stderr line naming that file' is exactly one line, so a missing and a non-list conflicts.json each warn once and never also emit a SWALLOW line — swallow is reserved for a present-but-unreadable narration/fold log and for a malformed JSONL row. No state exam in the Proof, so state.reached is left unset.","created_at":"2026-09-16T18:33:32.910224803Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T18:33:32.912Z"}
